{"title": "Mind Flayer Tadpole", "pageid": 19889, "url": "https://bg3.wiki/wiki/Mind_Flayer_Tadpole", "categories": ["Aberrations"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Mind Flayer Tadpoles</b> are <a href=\"/wiki/List_of_Creature_Types#Aberration\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"List of Creature Types\">Aberrations</a> used by the <a href=\"/wiki/Illithid\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Illithid\">Illithid</a> to transform <a href=\"/wiki/Humanoid\" title=\"Humanoid\">humanoids</a> into Illithids through the process of <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ceremorphosis\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/22px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/33px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/44px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Ceremorphosis\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/22px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-extlink\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ceremorphosis\">Ceremorphosis</a></span>. The player character and the origin companions of <i>Baldur's Gate 3</i> are infected with tadpoles. One of the first main <a href=\"/wiki/Quests\" title=\"Quests\">Quests</a> is to <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Find_a_Cure\" title=\"Find a Cure\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/22px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/33px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/44px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Find a Cure\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/22px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span>⁠<a href=\"/wiki/Find_a_Cure\" title=\"Find a Cure\">Find a Cure</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Involvement\">Involvement</span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Act_One\">Act One</span></h3>\n<p>It is revealed in <a href=\"/wiki/Act_One\" title=\"Act One\">Act One</a> that the <a href=\"/wiki/Cult_of_the_Absolute\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Cult of the Absolute\">Cult of the Absolute</a> is related to the Illithid abductions. By seeking out different healers to find a cure, the party can learn more about their affliction. It is also revealed that it is possible to absorb more <span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-story\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Mind_Flayer_Parasite_Specimen\" title=\"Mind Flayer Parasite Specimen\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/9/91/Mind_Flayer_Parasite_Specimen_Item_Icon.png/20px-Mind_Flayer_Parasite_Specimen_Item_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/9/91/Mind_Flayer_Parasite_Specimen_Item_Icon.png/30px-Mind_Flayer_Parasite_Specimen_Item_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/9/91/Mind_Flayer_Parasite_Specimen_Item_Icon.png/40px-Mind_Flayer_Parasite_Specimen_Item_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/9/91/Mind_Flayer_Parasite_Specimen_Item_Icon.png/20px-Mind_Flayer_Parasite_Specimen_Item_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/9/91/Mind_Flayer_Parasite_Specimen_Item_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Mind_Flayer_Parasite_Specimen\" title=\"Mind Flayer Parasite Specimen\">tadpoles</a>, unlocking <a href=\"/wiki/Illithid_Powers\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Illithid Powers\">Illithid Powers</a>.\n</p><p>If <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Auntie_Ethel\" title=\"Auntie Ethel\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/9/9e/Portrait_Ethel_Human.png/25px-Portrait_Ethel_Human.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/9/9e/Portrait_Ethel_Human.png/38px-Portrait_Ethel_Human.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/9/9e/Portrait_Ethel_Human.png/50px-Portrait_Ethel_Human.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Auntie Ethel\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/9/9e/Portrait_Ethel_Human.png/25px-Portrait_Ethel_Human.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/9/9e/Portrait_Ethel_Human.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Auntie_Ethel\" title=\"Auntie Ethel\">Auntie Ethel</a> or <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Halsin\" title=\"Halsin\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/f/fe/Portrait_Halsin.png/25px-Portrait_Halsin.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/f/fe/Portrait_Halsin.png/38px-Portrait_Halsin.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/f/fe/Portrait_Halsin.png/50px-Portrait_Halsin.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Halsin\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/f/fe/Portrait_Halsin.png/25px-Portrait_Halsin.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/f/fe/Portrait_Halsin.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Halsin\" title=\"Halsin\">Halsin</a> are spoken with, they reveal that the tadpoles are protected by shadow magic and cannot be removed by normal means. If initiating <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Help_Omeluum_Investigate_the_Parasite\" title=\"Help Omeluum Investigate the Parasite\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/22px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/33px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/44px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Help Omeluum Investigate the Parasite\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/22px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span>⁠<a href=\"/wiki/Help_Omeluum_Investigate_the_Parasite\" title=\"Help Omeluum Investigate the Parasite\">Help Omeluum Investigate the Parasite</a>, <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Omeluum\" title=\"Omeluum\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/7/7b/Portrait_Omeluum.png/25px-Portrait_Omeluum.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/7/7b/Portrait_Omeluum.png/38px-Portrait_Omeluum.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/7/7b/Portrait_Omeluum.png/50px-Portrait_Omeluum.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Omeluum\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/7/7b/Portrait_Omeluum.png/25px-Portrait_Omeluum.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/7/7b/Portrait_Omeluum.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Omeluum\" title=\"Omeluum\">Omeluum</a> reveals that the party's mind flayer parasites are held in stasis.\n</p><p>The <a href=\"/wiki/Dream_Visitor\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Dream Visitor\">Dream Visitor</a> ultimately visits the player character again in <a href=\"/wiki/Act_Two\" title=\"Act Two\">Act Two</a> and may inform them the order from the Absolute to trigger their <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Ceremorphosis\" title=\"Ceremorphosis\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/f/f8/Ceremorphosis_Icon.webp/25px-Ceremorphosis_Icon.webp, /w/images/thumb/f/f8/Ceremorphosis_Icon.webp/38px-Ceremorphosis_Icon.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/f/f8/Ceremorphosis_Icon.webp/50px-Ceremorphosis_Icon.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Ceremorphosis\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/f/f8/Ceremorphosis_Icon.webp/25px-Ceremorphosis_Icon.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/f/f8/Ceremorphosis_Icon.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Ceremorphosis\" title=\"Ceremorphosis\">Ceremorphosis</a> has been issued many times, but they have been blocking these orders.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Act_Two\">Act Two</span></h3>\n<p>Towards the end of Act Two, it is revealed that the tadpoles are largely produced in the <a href=\"/wiki/Mind_Flayer_Colony\" title=\"Mind Flayer Colony\">Mind Flayer Colony</a> beneath <a href=\"/wiki/Moonrise_Towers\" title=\"Moonrise Towers\">Moonrise Towers</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Mind_Flayer_Tadpole_(creature)\" title=\"Mind Flayer Tadpole (creature)\">Mind Flayer Tadpole (creature)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Illithid_Powers#Mind_flayer_parasite_locations\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Illithid Powers\">Mind Flayer Parasite Locations</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Mind_Flayer_Parasite_Specimen\" title=\"Mind Flayer Parasite Specimen\">Mind Flayer Parasite Specimen</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Illithid_Powers\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Illithid Powers\">Illithid Powers</a></li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ceremorphosis\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/22px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/33px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/44px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Ceremorphosis\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/22px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-extlink\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ceremorphosis\">Ceremorphosis</a></span> on the <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Main_Page\">Forgotten Realms Wiki</a></li></ul>\n<div class=\"navbox-styles\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r138587\">.mw-parser-output .hlist dl,.mw-parser-output .hlist ul,.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-horizontlist dl,.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-horizontlist ul{margin:0;padding:0}.mw-parser-output .hlist dl ul,.mw-parser-output .hlist dl dl,.mw-parser-output .hlist ul dl,.mw-parser-output .hlist ul ul,.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-horizontlist dl ul,.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-horizontlist dl dl,.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-horizontlist ul dl,.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-horizontlist ul ul{display:inline}.mw-parser-output .hlist dd,.mw-parser-output .hlist dt,.mw-parser-output .hlist li,.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-hor